{
  "version": 359,
  "released": "2026-09-25",
  "changelog": "v359: an answer outlives its card \u2014 an answer to a card that closed before it was placed now lands on the moment it was about, instead of being silently refused. WHERE IT WAS SEEN: the owner's own vault. He answered his father's mission card \"19-21 years old\" (`sources/conversations/msg-fc9845c47f8dc2b5099724a5.md`, `session_ref: conversation:cand:work_item:work:b7525efb7ce0bb69be2d7129`, captured 2026-09-23T02:36:54Z). Before the answer was placed, the 2026-09-23 resolver run dated that node from its own reading and v350's identity re-key moved it (`node:b69a5be503b14977a6ba0077` -> `node:80f419115b858c37a7b051f3` \"Father's mission to New Zealand\"), so the card left the published generation and v352's `place-answers` refused the answer `card_not_published`. On a scratch clone of his vault (generation 192), 20 OF THE 28 card answers were refused the same way, and the report showed only a count. THE CENSUS, from the vault's own publication history: all 20 were `card_not_published`, and that one name hid five fates \u2014 8 answers to 6 cards whose node another reading dated and whose id then re-keyed (the mission x3, \"Father's tenure as bishop\", \"Harvey's late talking start\", \"Isaac writes first check\", \"Investor apologizes and relationship recovers\", \"Castle Island final-stage rejection twice\"), 1 to a card that closed on the same node id when a classifier age dated it (\"Dad wins pet snake at fair\"), 3 to moments the resolver retracted as not an event (2 `duplicate`, 1 `fact_statement`), 6 to `missing_anchor` cards about an anchor handle (\"grandpa's death\", \"the move to Orderville\") the resolver has since bound, and 2 to an August contradiction card (\"Two dates are claimed for James's birth\") on a node the vault has since redrawn with no alias \u2014 both answers identity corrections (\"20th of March 1990 is AJ Taylor's birth\"). None was already reflected by an answer-placement receipt: the vault held none. THE PRINCIPLE (owner, via the brief): an answer the person gave to a question they were shown is testimony and must count; a card closing after it was shown must not void it. THE RULE (`answer_placement.AN_ANSWER_OUTLIVES_ITS_CARD`, one seat \u2014 `card_for_work_item`/`card_for_answer`, which both `place_answers` and `landmark_recorder.file_claims` call): a card the published generation no longer carries is RE-DERIVED from what it asked. A work id is `temporal_projection.derive_work_item_id` over (kind, subject, node, field), so `closed_cards` mints the ids every node the vault still holds could have been asked under \u2014 every drawn node with its resolved subjects and the raw `subject_mention` of every claim it folds (resolution is data about a claim, so the mention a card was minted from before v356 resolved it is still there), every id `node_aliases` redirects, and every `event_ref` a filed claim names \u2014 over `WORK_ITEM_KINDS` and every canonical field plus the one legacy spelling \u2014 `temporal_work_items.asked_work_item_ids`, beside `legacy_work_item_ids`, so `temporal_work_items` stays the only minter outside the projection (`test_work_item_aliases`' guard) and an id is re-minted rather than stored. Nothing is stored and nothing is read off an earlier publication. The node found is followed through `node_aliases` to where it is drawn NOW and the answer is placed there under that node's own subject, exactly as v352 places an answer to an open card. An `offered` card (shown, not yet answered) is answerable too. It is refused only when no node could have asked the card (`card_not_published`) or when the node it asked about is no longer drawn (`card_node_not_drawn`), and EVERY refused answer is now LISTED on the report (`unplaced`: source, work item, reason, and the asked node when known; `describe` prints each), with `through_a_closed_card` counted apart. WHAT v352 WAS PROTECTING, AND STILL IS: `card_not_open` stays for a published row a host marked `answered`/`resolved`/`dismissed`/`obsolete` (a decision recorded on the card; the fold never publishes one); an `unresolved:` subject is still refused; a card's node that is not drawn is still refused; one answer still files ONE receipt keyed on the reply's own revision, so a re-run writes nothing twice. ONE MORE DEFECT THE CLOSED CARDS SURFACED, IN THIS SEAT (lifehug#415 gap 1's shape): \"This would have happened, probably when I was 4 or 5\" answering \"When did Dad wins pet snake at fair happen?\" is the OWNER's age, and v352 would have filed it under the node's subject and measured it from his father's 1954 birth. `answer_placement.NARRATOR_AGE_RE` (a closed vocabulary: \"I was\", \"I'm\", \"we were\" before the age) files a first-person age as the narrator's (`self`), still on the card's node \u2014 the rule `aim_at_card` already keeps for a draft \u2014 so the fold measures it from the owner's own birth. The classifier-seat half of #415 (the \"Father's four years bedridden\" claim, `classifier_claims`/the classify prompt) is a different seat and stays filed. MEASURED on a scratch clone of the owner's vault (`/private/tmp/lifehug-rig-answers`, lifehug/dave at `bee67821`, generation 192, 1265 nodes; the original was never written to), one `migrate-classifier-moments` sweep per framework from the same commit. v358: 28 answers, 1 placed, 7 tellings, 20 refused `card_not_published`. v359: 28 answers, 4 placed, 13 tellings (9 of the 17 through a card that had closed), 11 refused and listed \u2014 8 `card_not_published` (the 6 anchor-card answers and the 2 August contradiction answers; 4 of the 8 were also heard by another reader whose claims are active) and 3 `card_node_not_drawn` naming `node:5273593ca6c107b65fd028bc` and `node:754698be980a0fbb8f202e5a`. Nodes 1278 and placed nodes 1228 under both. Cards 70 -> 71: `contradiction` 12 -> 13, every other kind unchanged (`precision_gap` 47, `missing_anchor` 6, `place_ambiguous` 2, `relation_word` 2, `identity_uncertain` 1). \"Father's mission to New Zealand\" now carries the answer's own `age` claim, subject `person/james-taylor`, measured 1973-06-04/1976-06-03 from 1954-06-04 (`age_corroborates_placement`) and joined to the placement's provenance; the drawn window stays the resolver's month-grained 1973-06/1976-06, basis anchor, because v345's ruling makes an AGREEING age evidence on a dated moment and never its rival (on a node nothing else dated, the answer alone places it 1973-06-04/1976-06-03, basis age \u2014 pinned in the test). The v340/v342 LOST-PLACEMENT AUDIT: `lost` and `drawn_at_an_alias` EMPTY; `moved` names ONE node, `node:55b4d58109978a433c069fbe` \"Dad wins pet snake at fair\", 1959~ -> 1985~ \u2014 the owner's own answer placing it by his own age, over a classifier reading that filed \"I must have been like four or five years old\" as his father's (the same #415 shape); the 1959 reading is kept as the alternate and the one new card asks \"Two dates are claimed for Dad wins pet snake at fair \u2014 around 1985 and around 1959. Which is right?\". `CALCULATION_RULE_VERSION` DOES NOT MOVE (`timeline-rules:18`): this release files claims an answer was owed and changes no derivation; a vault with no closed-card answer draws exactly what it drew. GUARDS: `tests/test_v359_an_answer_outlives_its_card.py` \u2014 the owner's real ids (`work:b7525efb7ce0bb69be2d7129` is proved to be the digest of precision_gap / \"James Edwin Taylor\" / `node:b69a5be503b14977a6ba0077` / date, and re-derives to `node:80f419115b858c37a7b051f3` through the alias), the defect reproduced without the derivation, the alias and the raw mention each proved necessary, a retired node re-deriving to the right refusal, the legacy field, a published card never read as closed, `offered` answerable and the settled states still refused; end to end on a synthetic vault minted by the real minter, in the incident's order (card shown, resolver dates the node, card leaves, answer arrives): the answer placed on the node under the node's subject, joined to the placement, the audit empty, idempotent, a dry run writing nothing, the sweep carrying it, and the listener seat aiming its \"they\" draft at the closed card; the answer alone placing 1973-06-04/1976-06-03; both refusals listed; the narrator's age measured from the owner's birth. Every guard was run with its rule removed and SEEN failing.",
